WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.787
Some simple views can be updated directly.

00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:08.802
If a view is based on one table and keeps a clear one to one relationship with the underlying rows,

00:00:08.802 --> 00:00:13.307
Postgres may allow an update through the view to change the base table.

00:00:13.307 --> 00:00:16.272
But this does not apply to every view.

00:00:16.272 --> 00:00:23.587
A view with joins, grouping, or aggregate calculations may not have a clear single source row to update.

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:28.549
So treat write behavior as something you verify, not something you assume.
